            One recovery point with its details; a snapshot lists its members (first page). A point the caller can't\
             read is not_found.
            """
        case .recoveryList:
            """
            Recovery points of a vault, or of one path (a file's history or the points under a directory): local\
             snapshots, local versions and provider versions. Points the caller can't read are omitted.\
             refresh_provider lists the provider's versions first (metadata only, request-budgeted).
            """
        case .recoveryPlan:
            """
            Plan a restore (read-only): recovery_id, or vault_id + path + at for a point-in-time reconstruction (never\
             atomic; see consistency_note). Returns the per-item preview, estimate, warnings, blockers and the token\
             recovery.restore takes (stored 30 minutes).
            """
        case .recoveryPlanGet:
            "A stored restore plan (its state, items and token)."
        case .recoveryPointDelete:
            """
            Delete a snapshot or a local version (filesystem Delete on its path). A refusal with data.code\
             'recovery_point_delete' asks for confirmation: resend with confirm.
            """
        case .recoveryRestore:
            """
            Run a restore plan: every item is re-authorized and restored as a new current generation; a destination\
             that changed since the plan is a 'conflict' outcome. Resumable. Refusals: 'recovery_restore' (token\
             missing or expired: plan again), 'recovery_unverified_version' (resend with accept_unverified).
            """
        case .recoverySnapshotCreate:
            """
            Take a named local snapshot of a file or directory tree (vault mode local_snapshots). Needs Read + Copy on\
             every file and List on every directory of the subtree.
            """
        case .roleVaultAssign:
            "Assign a vault role to a user or group on a vault (one assignment per subject and vault)."
        case .roleVaultGet:
            "One vault role definition."
        case .roleVaultUnassign:
            "Remove a subject's vault role assignment on a vault."
        case .rolesVaultList:
            "Every vault role definition."
        case .rolesVaultListAssigned:
            "The role assignments on one vault (id is the vault id)."
        case .shareLinkCreate:
            "Create a share link on a file or directory. The public token is returned once."
        case .shareLinkRevoke:
            "Revoke a share link; its sessions end on their next request."
        case .storageVaultAdd:
            """
            Create a vault. owner_id, description and quota (bytes, 0 = unlimited) are optional; the daemon picks the\
             backing directory. S3 vaults also need api_key_id and bucket. A refusal with data.code\
             'encryption_waiver' means the bucket already holds data: resend with accept_encryption_waiver once the\
             person accepts. With provision (#237) the daemon creates a managed bucket or adopts an existing one;\
             'upstream_adoption' asks for provision.accept_adoption.
            """
        case .storageVaultGet:
            "One vault with its owner's name (and sync policy for S3 vaults)."
        case .storageVaultList:
            "Vaults visible to the caller; each row carries the owner's name."
        case .storageVaultRemove:
            """
            Delete a vault: restorable until the retention window ends, or purged on the next pass with `now`.\
             Refusals with data.code 'vault_upstream_key_loss' (resend with accept_key_loss) or 'vault_delete_now'\
             (resend with confirm_now).
            """
        case .upstreamAdminDisable:
            "Turn provider administration off. Refused while an event subscription runs through the key."
        case .upstreamAdminEnable:
            """
            Turn on provider administration (AWS S3, Cloudflare R2) for an upstream API key after probing it, or store\
             / clear the Cloudflare API token R2 events need. Idempotent. Needs admin.upstream.configure + key edit.
            """
        case .upstreamAdminStatus:
            "Administration status and the last capability probe; probe=true re-checks the credential (configure)."
        case .upstreamAuditList:
            "Upstream control-plane audit log (newest first): locks, creations, adoptions, lifecycle, events, cleanup."
        case .upstreamBucketAdoptPreflight:
            """
            Read-only admission check of an existing bucket before adoption: object counts, encryption of a sample,\
             versioning, object lock, Vaulthalla manifest, blockers.
            """
        case .upstreamBucketCleanup:
            """
            Delete every object version of a bucket Vaulthalla created and (delete_bucket, default) the bucket. Every\
             check runs again first. A refusal with data.code 'upstream_cleanup' means the token is missing, expired\
             or no longer matches the bucket: run the preflight again.
            """
        case .upstreamBucketCleanupPreflight:
            """
            What cleanup would delete (objects, versions, delete markers, bytes) and anything that blocks it, with a\
             confirm_token valid for 10 minutes. Nothing changes.
            """
        case .upstreamBucketDetach:
            "Give a managed or adopted bucket that no vault uses back: Vaulthalla removes its own rules; data stays."
        case .upstreamBucketInspect:
            "Bucket configuration: region, versioning, object lock, lifecycle and notification rules (ours vs foreign)."
        case .upstreamBucketLifecycleSet:
            """
            Set or clear Vaulthalla's lifecycle rule on a managed or adopted bucket; foreign rules are preserved.\
             Expiration is destructive: a refusal with data.code 'upstream_destructive_lifecycle' asks for\
             accept_destructive.
            """
        case .upstreamBucketList:
            """
            One page of the account's buckets (ListBuckets) merged with what Vaulthalla knows: managed, adopted,\
             unmanaged or protected. No bucket-level or object calls.
            """
        case .upstreamBucketProtect:
            "Lock a bucket: Vaulthalla will not probe, adopt, bind, configure, sync, empty or delete it. Audited."
        case .upstreamBucketUnprotect:
            """
            Remove a bucket lock (admin.upstream.unprotect). A refusal with data.code 'upstream_unprotect' asks for\
             confirmation: resend with confirm.
            """
        case .upstreamEventsDisable:
            "Remove the vault's event rule (and the queue when nothing else uses it and Vaulthalla created it)."
        case .upstreamEventsEnable:
            "Subscribe an S3 vault's bucket for event-driven sync (AWS S3 → SQS, Cloudflare R2 → Queues)."
        case .upstreamEventsRepair:
            "Re-create whatever is missing for the vault's subscription and re-arm it. Safe to repeat."
        case .upstreamEventsStatus:
            """
            Event subscription, queue health and inbox counts for one vault (vault_id) or every S3 vault the caller\
             may view. A vault without a subscription reports state 'none'.
            """
        case .vaultRecoveryDisclosure:
            """
            The cost disclosure a person must see before provider versioning is enabled, with the token\
             vault.recovery.update needs (10 minutes). Read-only: at most one admin inspect, no object requests.
            """
        case .vaultRecoveryStatus:
            """
            A vault's recovery mode, local versioning, store usage, upstream backlog and provider versioning state;\
             refresh_provider re-reads the bucket (one admin round trip).
            """
        case .vaultRecoverySuspend:
            """
            Suspend versioning on the vault's bucket; existing versions are kept and nothing is deleted. A refusal\
             with data.code 'recovery_versioning_suspend' asks for confirmation: resend with confirm.
            """
        case .vaultRecoveryUpdate:
            """
            Change a vault's recovery settings. mode provider_versioning needs disclosure_token from\
             vault.recovery.disclosure ('recovery_versioning_disclosure'); unpriced costs need accept_unpriced\
             ('recovery_versioning_unpriced'); a shorter retention needs accept_retention_shortening\
             ('recovery_retention_shorten'); the vault's unmanaged bucket needs accept_adoption ('upstream_adoption').
            """
        }
    }
}

